                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "title": "When the H&P Saves the Patient",
                  "content": "Sometimes the H&P doesn't just document care — it **changes** care.\n\n**Real case**: 47-year-old woman admitted for elective laparoscopic cholecystectomy. Pre-op H&P performed by surgeon noted:\n• **FH**: Mother and maternal aunt both had \"high fever after surgery and died.\"\n• **PSH**: Patient had never had general anesthesia.\n• **Plan**: Surgeon recognized the **family history of malignant hyperthermia (MH)** — a hereditary, life-threatening reaction to volatile anesthetics and succinylcholine.\n\nThe surgeon **delayed surgery**, ordered an anesthesia consult, and arranged for a **non-triggering anesthetic technique** (TIVA — total intravenous anesthesia without volatile agents). Dantrolene was confirmed on-hand. Family was referred for genetic counseling.\n\nThe patient had an uneventful operation. Without that single FH question, succinylcholine would have been administered, MH crisis would have developed within minutes, and the family's tragic history would have repeated.\n\n**The H&P isn't paperwork.** It's the first and most powerful screening tool in inpatient medicine. Three minutes of questioning prevented a death.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">WHEN THE H&amp;P SAVES A LIFE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">A family history catch</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">THE PATIENT</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"285\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">47 y/o F  elective laparoscopic chole</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"325\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">No prior general anesthesia exposure</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"410\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"470\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">FH CLUE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"515\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Mother &amp; aunt: high fever after surgery, died</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Classic malignant hyperthermia history</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"640\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">RECOGNITION</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"745\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Surgeon delayed surgery, consulted anesthesia</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"785\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Plan changed to TIVA  no triggering agents</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"870\" width=\"940\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"930\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">OUTCOME</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"975\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Uneventful surgery  family genetic counseling</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1015\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">A single FH question prevented a death</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "The H&P as a life-saving screening tool"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "application",
                  "title": "How to Audit an H&P in 5 Minutes",
                  "content": "When you're working concurrent record review, you need a **fast audit method** for H&P compliance. Run this **5-minute checklist**:\n\n1. **Timeliness** — Was the H&P completed within 24 hours of admission AND before any anesthesia procedure? Check timestamp.\n\n2. **Authentication** — Is the H&P signed (electronic signature or wet signature), dated, AND timed by the responsible practitioner? Co-signature for resident/NP/PA if applicable?\n\n3. **All 7 components present?** CC, HPI, ROS, PMH, FH, SH, PE — each section identifiable in the document?\n\n4. **HPI quality** — At least 4 OLDCARTS elements OR status of 3+ chronic conditions documented?\n\n5. **Update note present?** If H&P >24 hours old at admission, is there an update note with new findings (or \"no changes\") within 24 hours?\n\nDeficiency = enter into chart deficiency system and notify physician within 24 hours. Repeat deficiencies trigger automatic privilege suspension per medical staff bylaws (typically after 14-30 days of unresolved deficiencies).",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">H&amp;P 5-MINUTE AUDIT</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Concurrent record review checklist</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"180\" width=\"900\" height=\"130\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"245\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">1.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"245\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Timeliness  24 hours AND before anesthesia</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"285\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Check admission and H&amp;P timestamps</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"330\" width=\"900\" height=\"130\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"395\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">2.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"395\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Authentication  signed, dated, timed</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"435\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Co-signature for resident/NP/PA per state</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"480\" width=\"900\" height=\"130\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"545\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">3.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"545\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">All 7 components present and labeled</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"585\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">CC HPI ROS PMH FH SH PE+A/P</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"630\" width=\"900\" height=\"130\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"695\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">4.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"695\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">HPI quality  4+ OLDCARTS or 3+ chronic</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"735\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Drives the E/M leveling defensibility</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"780\" width=\"900\" height=\"130\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"845\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">5.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"845\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Update note if H&amp;P &gt;24h old at admit</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"885\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Within 24h AND before anesthesia</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"930\" width=\"900\" height=\"120\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"985\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Any failure  deficiency notice within 24h</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1020\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Repeat deficiency  privilege suspension per bylaws</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "A repeatable concurrent audit playbook"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "quiz",
                  "question": "Per CMS 1995 E/M guidelines, a Comprehensive ROS requires documentation of how many of the 14 recognized body systems?",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "text": "All 14 systems must be explicitly documented in every encounter",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "10 or more systems must be reviewed and documented (positives or pertinent negatives count)",
                      "correct": true
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "5 systems is sufficient for any inpatient comprehensive H&P",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Only the systems directly related to the chief complaint count toward ROS",
                      "correct": false
                    }
                  ],
                  "explanation": "CMS 1995/1997 E/M guidelines define a Complete ROS as documentation of 10 or more body systems. Both positive findings AND pertinent negatives count — for example, 'denies fever, chills, weight loss' (constitutional) is one full system. A documented statement like 'all other systems reviewed and negative' is accepted by CMS when at least the systems related to the problem are individually addressed. The 14 systems are: constitutional, eyes, ENT, CV, respiratory, GI, GU, MSK, skin, neuro, psych, endocrine, heme/lymph, allergic/immuno.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">ROS levels  CMS 1995/1997</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">PROBLEM PERTINENT</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"280\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">1 system  directly related to CC</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"315\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Expanded problem-focused level</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"350\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"405\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">EXTENDED</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"450\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">2-9 systems documented</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Detailed level</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"520\" width=\"940\" height=\"220\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"575\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">COMPLETE  10+ SYSTEMS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"620\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Required for COMPREHENSIVE history</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"660\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">99222 / 99223 Initial Hospital Care</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Pertinent positives AND negatives count</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"770\" width=\"940\" height=\"270\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"825\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">14 SYSTEMS RECOGNIZED</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"875\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Constitutional Eyes ENT CV Resp GI GU MSK</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"915\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Skin Neuro Psych Endo Heme/Lymph Immuno</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"975\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">all other systems reviewed and negative accepted</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"1005\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">when problem-related systems are individually addressed</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "10+ systems for Comprehensive ROS"
                  }
                }
